  <h2>About agriculture procurement</h2>
  <p>
    Agriculture-sector tenders are issued by the national Department of Agriculture, Land Reform and Rural
    Development, provincial agriculture departments, the Agricultural Research Council, and the Land Bank,
    alongside agri-related procurement from district and local municipalities. Recurring categories include
    fencing, boreholes and irrigation, veterinary services, extension services, fresh produce market
    infrastructure, and post-harvest cold-chain facilities.
  </p>

  <h2>Detailed sector hub — coming soon</h2>
  <p>
    We're building a detailed agriculture-sector hub covering the major procuring entities, the recurring
    tender categories, the compliance requirements (SAVC registration for veterinary services, environmental
    authorisations, water-use licences), and the link between sector codes (AgriBEE) and PPPFA specific goals.
    Join the waitlist below to be notified when it publishes.
  </p>

  <p>
    In the meantime, the
    <a href="https://www.etenders.gov.za" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">eTenders Publication Portal</a>
    carries all current agriculture-sector tenders.
  </p>
